                <pb facs="0866" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/2625: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Heath</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-08T13:00:00-05:00">April 8, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. The Haitian Minister of Finance intends to re-submit to the Legislature the
                    permanent finance law drafted by the Financial Adviser and transmitted to the
                    Department in the Legation’s despatch No. 483 of August 29, 1932.<anchor n="86"
                        xml:id="d701-f1"/> The Minister, however, proposes to omit the special
                    article 36 which confirms the powers of the Financial Adviser now exercised by
                    virtue of the Treaty of 1915<anchor n="87" xml:id="d701-f2"/> and existing
                    accords until the “liquidation” of those instruments. He says that it would be
                    impossible to get the Legislature to vote this article but that the Government
                    will confirm these powers in a note to the Legation employing the same language
                    as that of the article in question.</p>
                <p>I recommend that the Financial Adviser be authorized to approve this law upon the
                    condition that the Haitian Government will confirm in writing the powers
                    mentioned in article 36.</p>
                <p>Please instruct by cable since the budget, of which the finance law forms a part,
                    is to be submitted to the Legislature in accordance with the constitution early
                    next week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Heath</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
